\f1\b SharedUI Extraction Candidates \'97 Analysis
\f0\b0                                                                    \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b 1. Gallery Layout (\cf3 AppKitGalleryLayout\cf2 )
\f0\b0                                                                      \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Near-identical. Both apps define a private \cf3 AppKitGalleryLayout: NSCollectionViewFlowLayout\cf2  with \
  the same column-count-driven grid logic, same insets (18/18/18/18), same spacing (14 horizontal, 16\
  vertical), same \cf3 prepare()\cf2  override computing \cf3 itemSize\cf2  from \cf3 columnCount\cf2 . The only difference is Ledger adds  \
  \cf3 titleHeight + titleGap\cf2  to the item height for filename labels below thumbnails.                           \
                                               \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Extract to SharedUI with an optional \cf3 extraItemHeight: CGFloat = 0\cf2  parameter (Ledger passes  \
  \cf3 titleGap + titleHeight\cf2 , Librarian passes 0).\
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0                                                                                                        \
  - Eliminates ~50 lines of duplicate layout code\
  - Ensures both apps use identical grid spacing, so galleries feel consistent                                \
  - Bug fixes to column sizing logic apply to both apps at once                                             \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0 \
  - Very low complexity \'97 the duplication is small and unlikely to drift                                      \
  - Ledger's title-height addition is a minor but real divergence that slightly complicates the shared version\
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Do it
\f0\b0  \'97 low effort, meaningful consistency gain.                                                   \
                                                                                                              \
  ---                                                                                                         \
  
\f1\b 2. Gallery Collection View (\cf3 AppKitGalleryCollectionView\cf2 )
\f0\b0                                                     \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  High but not identical. Both override \cf3 mouseDown\cf2  (background click, modified click), \cf3 keyDown\cf2 \
  (escape, arrow keys), and have the same closure-based callback pattern (\cf3 onBackgroundClick\cf2 , \cf3 onMoveSelection\cf2 , \
  \cf3 onModifiedItemClick\cf2 ). Ledger adds \cf3 contextMenuProvider\cf2 , \cf3 onDoubleClick\cf2 , \cf3 onActivateSelection\cf2  and handles     \
  Shift+arrow natively. Librarian handles Shift+arrow via the \cf3 onMoveSelection\cf2  closure's \cf3 Bool\cf2                   \
  extending-selection param.                                                                                \
                                               \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Extract to SharedUI with the union of all callbacks. Apps only wire the ones they use.      \
   \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0                                                                                                        \
  - Eliminates ~70 lines of duplicate mouse/keyboard handling                                               \
  - Standardises selection interaction model                                                                  \
   \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0                                                                                                        \
  - Ledger's \cf3 onMoveSelection\cf2  takes \cf3 (MoveCommandDirection)\cf2  while Librarian's takes \cf3 (MoveCommandDirection, Bool)\cf2 \
   \'97 the signatures differ. Need a unified callback signature.                                                \
  - Ledger passes all keyboard events to super when modifiers are present; Librarian only passes Shift+arrow\
  through its \cf3 onMoveSelection\cf2  callback. Merging these requires careful thought about which keyboard guard is  \
  correct.                                                                                                    \
                                               \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Do it
\f0\b0  \'97 but carefully unify the \cf3 onMoveSelection\cf2  signature (probably \cf3 (MoveCommandDirection, Bool)\cf2    \
  with Ledger ignoring the Bool).                                                                             \
                                               \
  ---                                                                                                         \
  
\f1\b 3. \cf3 MoveCommandDirection\cf2  enum
\f0\b0                                                                               \
                                               \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Identical in both apps \'97 \cf3 .left, .right, .up, .down\cf2 .\
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Extract to SharedUI alongside the gallery collection view.                                  \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0  Trivial extraction, removes duplication.                                                              \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0  None.                                                                                               \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Do it
\f0\b0  \'97 free win.                                                                                \
                                                                                                              \
  ---                                                                                                       \
  
\f1\b 4. \cf3 KeyCode\cf2  constants
\f0\b0                          \
                      \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Ledger defines a proper \cf3 KeyCode\cf2  enum. Librarian uses hardcoded \cf3 UInt16\cf2  values (e.g., \cf3 53\cf2  for\
  Escape, \cf3 123\cf2 \'96\cf3 126\cf2  for arrows).                                                                                \
   \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Extract Ledger's \cf3 KeyCode\cf2  enum to SharedUI. Librarian adopts it, replacing magic numbers.    \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0                                                                                                        \
  - Improves Librarian's readability significantly                                                          \
  - Both apps reference same constant names                                                                   \
   \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0  None.                                                                                                 \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Do it
\f0\b0  \'97 trivial, immediate readability improvement for Librarian.                                  \
                                                                                                            \
  ---                                                                                                         \
  
\f1\b 5. Toolbar Spinner Item
\f0\b0                                                                                    \
                                               \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Identical. Both apps create an \cf3 NSProgressIndicator\cf2  with \cf3 .spinning\cf2  style, \cf3 .small\cf2  control size,\
  \cf3 isDisplayedWhenStopped = false\cf2 , wrapped in a 16\'d716 container with centered constraints, assigned to an      \
  \cf3 NSToolbarItem\cf2  with \cf3 .low\cf2  visibility priority.\
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Extract a factory function: \cf3 makeToolbarSpinnerItem(identifier:) -> (item: NSToolbarItem, \cf2    \
  \cf3 spinner: NSProgressIndicator)\cf2 .               \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0                                                                                                      \
  - Eliminates ~20 lines of identical boilerplate per app\
  - Ensures spinner appearance is consistent                                                                  \
   \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0                                                                                                        \
  - It's a factory for one specific item type \'97 slightly over-specific for a shared library                 \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Do it
\f0\b0  \'97 small but clean. Both apps need it, the code is identical.\
                                                                                                              \
  ---                                                                                                       \
  
\f1\b 6. Toolbar Inspector Toggle Item
\f0\b0                                                                             \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Very similar. Both create an \cf3 NSToolbarItem\cf2  with \cf3 sidebar.trailing\cf2  symbol, \cf3 autovalidates = false\cf2 ,\
  targeting \cf3 toggleInspector(_:)\cf2 . Label updates to "Show/Hide Inspector" based on state.                       \
   \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Extract a factory: \cf3 makeInspectorToggleToolbarItem(identifier:target:action:) -> \cf2             \
  \cf3 NSToolbarItem\cf2 .                                                                                            \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0  Small duplication removed, consistent appearance.                                                     \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0  Minimal \'97 both apps already do this in ~8 lines.\
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Maybe
\f0\b0  \'97 low priority, the duplication is small.                                                  \
                                                                                                              \
  ---                                                                                                       \
  
\f1\b 7. Toolbar Zoom In/Out Items
\f0\b0                  \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Identical. Both create \cf3 NSToolbarItem\cf2  with \cf3 minus\cf2 /\cf3 plus\cf2  symbols, same labels, \cf3 autovalidates = \cf2 \
  \cf3 false\cf2 .                                                                                                      \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Extract factory: \cf3 makeZoomToolbarItem(identifier:direction:target:action:) -> NSToolbarItem\cf2 . \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0  Removes ~20 lines of duplication.                                                                     \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0  Very thin wrapper.                                                                                  \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Maybe
\f0\b0  \'97 could bundle with the spinner factory into a \cf3 ToolbarItemFactory\cf2  enum.                      \
                                               \
  ---                                                                                                         \
  
\f1\b 8. NSAlert Sheet/Modal Helper
\f0\b0                                                                              \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Both apps repeat the same pattern in 4+ places: build an \cf3 NSAlert\cf2 , then \cf3 if let window \{ \cf2 \
  \cf3 alert.beginSheetModal(for: window) \{ ... \} \} else \{ alert.runModal() \}\cf2 . Ledger's \cf3 applicationShouldTerminate\cf2  \
  and Librarian's archive confirmation both use this exact pattern.                                         \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Extract an extension on \cf3 NSAlert\cf2 :                                                            \
  \cf4 extension NSAlert \cf2 \{                          \
      \cf4 func\cf5  runSheetOrModal(for window: \cf6 NSWindow\cf5 ?, completion: \cf4 @escaping\cf5  (\cf6 NSApplication\cf5 .\cf6 ModalResponse\cf5 ) -> \cf6 Void\cf5 )\cf2 \
      \cf4 func\cf5  runSheetOrModal(for window: \cf6 NSWindow\cf5 ?)\cf2  \cf4 async\cf2  -> \cf6 NSApplication\cf2 .\cf6 ModalResponse\cf2                         \
  \}                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0                                                                                                        \
  - Eliminates the most-repeated boilerplate in both apps (the if/else window check)                          \
  - The async variant is especially useful \'97 Librarian already uses \cf3 withCheckedContinuation\cf2  for this          \
  - Reduces 8\'9612 lines per alert to 1\'962                                                             \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0                                                                                                        \
  - Very thin wrapper \'97 some developers prefer to see the explicit flow                                       \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Do it
\f0\b0  \'97 high value, used everywhere, and the async variant is genuinely useful.                    \
                                                                                                              \
  ---                                                                                                       \
  
\f1\b 9. Pinch-to-Zoom Gesture Handler
\f0\b0                                                                             \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Both apps install \cf3 NSMagnificationGestureRecognizer\cf2  and use the same accumulator pattern with a\
  threshold (both use 0.14). The logic is identical: accumulate delta, fire column adjustment when threshold  \
  exceeded, reset on gesture end.\
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Extract a reusable \cf3 PinchZoomHandler\cf2  class or a protocol extension.                          \
                                               \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0                                                                                                        \
  - ~30 lines of identical logic shared                                                                     \
  - Both apps use the same threshold value                                                                    \
   \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0                                                                                                        \
  - The handler is tightly coupled to each app's zoom model (\cf3 model.adjustGalleryGridLevel\cf2  vs                \
  \cf3 model.canIncreaseGalleryZoom\cf2 ). Abstracting it requires a callback interface.                                \
  - Only used once per app                                                                                  \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Maybe
\f0\b0  \'97 the abstraction cost is slightly high for ~30 lines. Could bundle with the gallery       \
  collection view if that gets extracted.                                                                     \
   \
  ---                                                                                                         \
  
