\f0\b0                                                                                        \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Both apps define \cf3 thumbnailCornerRadius: 8\cf2 , \cf3 imageInset: 4\cf2 , and the same selection-background\
  styling pattern. Ledger has additional list-view metrics that are Ledger-specific.                          \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  Add gallery metrics to SharedUI alongside the gallery layout:                               \
  \cf4 public\cf2  \cf4 enum GalleryMetrics \cf2 \{                                                                              \
      \cf4 public\cf2  \cf4 static\cf2  \cf4 let\cf2  thumbnailCornerRadius: \cf6 CGFloat\cf2  = \cf7 8\cf2                                                     \
      \cf4 public\cf2  \cf4 static\cf2  \cf4 let\cf2  imageInset: \cf6 CGFloat\cf2  = \cf7 4\cf2                                                                \
      \cf4 public\cf2  \cf4 static\cf2  \cf4 let\cf2  gridInsets = \cf6 NSEdgeInsets\cf2 (top: \cf7 18\cf2 , left: \cf7 18\cf2 , bottom: \cf7 18\cf2 , right: \cf7 18\cf2 )                   \
      \cf4 public\cf2  \cf4 static\cf2  \cf4 let\cf2  horizontalSpacing: \cf6 CGFloat\cf2  = \cf7 14\cf2                                                        \
      \cf4 public\cf2  \cf4 static\cf2  \cf4 let\cf2  verticalSpacing: \cf6 CGFloat\cf2  = \cf7 16\cf2                                                          \
  \}                                                                                                           \
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Pros:
\f0\b0  Consistent visual appearance, single source of truth.                                                 \
  
\f1\b Cons:
\f0\b0  Only meaningful if the gallery layout is also extracted.                                              \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Do it
\f0\b0  \'97 but only as part of the gallery layout extraction.                                         \
                                                                                                            \
  ---                                                                                                         \
  
\f1\b 11. Gallery Item (NSCollectionViewItem subclass)
\f0\b0                                                           \
                                                  \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Both apps have custom \cf3 NSCollectionViewItem\cf2  subclasses with the same structure: selection\
  background view, centered image view with corner radius, aspect-ratio-aware sizing, \cf3 prepareForReuse\cf2  cleanup.\
   Ledger adds a title label and pending-edit dot. Librarian has a fallback symbol image.\
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Don't extract.
\f0\b0  The visual requirements are too different \'97 Ledger shows filename + pending  \
  dot, Librarian shows photo-only tiles with a fallback icon. The shared part (image centering, corner radius,\
   selection highlight) is layout code that doesn't lend itself well to a configurable base class.            \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Pros of extracting:
\f0\b0  Would standardise selection highlight and corner radius.                                \
  
\f1\b Cons of extracting:
\f0\b0  Would require extensive configuration points (title label yes/no, pending dot yes/no,\
  fallback image yes/no), making the "shared" class harder to maintain than two simple independent classes.   \
                                                                                                            \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Don't do it
\f0\b0  \'97 the divergences outweigh the common parts.                                           \
                                                                                                            \
  ---                                                                                                         \
  
\f1\b 12. Toolbar Installation Pattern
\f0\b0                                                                           \
                                               \
  
\f1\b Similarity:
\f0\b0  Both apps have a \cf3 installMainToolbar(on:resetDelegateState:)\cf2  method that creates an \cf3 NSToolbar\cf2 ,\
  sets \cf3 displayMode = .iconOnly\cf2 , \cf3 allowsUserCustomization = false\cf2 , \cf3 autosavesConfiguration = false\cf2 , assigns the  \
  delegate, and attaches to the window. The code is ~8 lines per app.\
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Recommendation:
\f0\b0  
\f1\b Don't extract.
\f0\b0  The toolbar identifier and delegate reference are app-specific, and the      \
  pattern is only 8 lines. A shared helper wouldn't meaningfully reduce code.\
                                                                                                              \
  
\f1\b Verdict: Don't do it
\f0\b0  \'97 too thin to justify.                                                                 \
                                               \
  ---                                                                                                         \
  
